From e0cfdd2cd2add9e63f74d785e38623896419d90d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Woolley <rob.woolley@windriver.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 13:33:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] boards/px4/fmu-v6x: enable SIH and force quad-X SIH airframe

Enables CONFIG_MODULES_SIMULATION_SIMULATOR_SIH=y (PX4's onboard
flight-dynamics simulation module) and forces SYS_AUTOSTART=1100
(the existing 1100_rc_quad_x_sih.hil airframe) as the effective
default every boot, since there is no persistent parameter storage
in this environment for a runtime `param set` to survive a reboot.

Also disables real-hardware drivers/modules made redundant by SIH's
own simulated backends (SENSOR_BARO_SIM/GPS_SIM/MAG_SIM, PWM_OUT_SIM)
and by this variant only ever running the quad-X (1100) airframe:
all real IMU/barometer/magnetometer chip drivers, UAVCAN, camera/
gimbal/OSD peripherals, differential pressure (airspeed), and
fixed-wing/VTOL flight control modules. This is a real, necessary
fix, not just cleanup: with SIH added, the unmodified default.px4board
overflows fmu-v6x's FLASH region by 47052 bytes (confirmed via a real
build failure), and none of the removed items do anything useful in
this environment anyway (M3's own boot log already showed every real
sensor driver reporting "no device on bus").

This patch is carried only by px4-firmware-renode (a distinct,
Renode-only build variant, specs/004-sih-renode-mavlink.md); the
real hardware build (px4-firmware) is unaffected.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific, Renode-only testing variant]

Signed-off-by: Rob Woolley <rob.woolley@windriver.com>
---
 boards/px4/fmu-v6x/default.px4board       | 31 +----------------------
 boards/px4/fmu-v6x/init/rc.board_defaults | 10 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

